      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Valley of Lunanyn [zone=807]\n**Who:**\n- Geirdan Ath [npc=38147]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Algot Yor [npc=38154]\n- Egot Mek [npc=38153]\n- Hemot Talas [npc=38280]\n- a mosstrooper [npc=38263]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Lunanyn #1: Raid and Recover [quest=5395]\n- Lunanyn #3: Uncharted Territory [quest=5419]\n- Lunanyn #4: The Enemy of My Enemy [quest=5420]\n- Lunanyn #5: The Memory Remains [quest=5421]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 16 02:37:15 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the second in a series of five; a solo task that begins with Geirdan Ath in the Valley of Lunanyn, located at 2295, -1700, 46 (in a building in the southeast part of the upper section of the zone)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"Raid and Recover\"\n\\- (no minimum required skill level in Alaran Language)\nYou say, 'Hail, Geirdan Ath'\nGeirdan Ath says 'I am glad to have you back. Your [help] was much appreciated last time. Our occupation here is important in finding out what happened to Cazic Thule and who stole his power. But until then, these farmers are causing some problems for us. Their involvement makes it more difficult than necessary in our fight against the Prophet's Army. Perhaps they can be [convinced] that our fight is not with them.'\nYou say, 'Convinced?'\nGeirdan Ath says 'You may have to be... blunt... in the manner in which you convince them of this. But I trust you can find a way. Unless your [stomach] is not in this.'\nYou say, 'My stomach's in it'\nGeirdan Ath says 'Excellent! There are three leaders that you must deal with. Egot Mek, Algot Yor, and Hemot Talas. Once they are dealt with, I am sure the others will fall in line. '\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Assassination Game'.\nGeirdan Ath is concerned about the farmers within the valley. Although they share a common enemy, the farmers still choose to fight the Rallosian forces. They pray to nature to create barbarous mosstroopers, which make it difficult to concentrate on the Prophet's army itself. Perhaps if the farmers had no leadership, it would convince them to give up the fight against Geirdan's army.\nPerhaps you can convince Egot Mek to lay down alir arms. Al tends the land high in the northwestern terraces.\n\n---\n\n_You'll have to hail and kill three named farmers in the northwestern boundary part of the zone._\n_NOTE: If you have multiple people in the same party doing this task at the same, you can prevent non-update issues by doing the hails while everyone is invisible, then breaking the invis to kill the mob._\nSpeak to Egot Mek 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nKill Egot Mek 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak to Algot Yor 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nKill Algot Yor 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak to Hemot Talas 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nKill Hemot Talas 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak to Geirdan Ath 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nYou say, 'Hail, Geirdan Ath'\nGeirdan Ath says 'Excellent work! Now kill those moss troopers they have been creating. Thinning their number should help quite a bit.'\nKill 4 mosstroopers 0/4 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak to Geirdan Ath 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nYou say, 'Hail, Geirdan Ath'\nGeirdan Ath says 'Perhaps now these farmers will cooperate! '\nYou were able to put a stop to the raiders and have freed the missing soldiers, at least until more their reinforcements can arrive. With fewer moss troopers around, it should make traveling a bit easier for his men.\n_Rewards:_\nEltarki's Diary - Life and Death\n- Eltarki's Diary - Life and Death [item=98146]",
