      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Valley of Lunanyn [zone=807]\n**Who:**\n- Geirdan Ath [npc=38147]\nRating:\n0/3**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(Average from 3 ratings)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a missing soldier [npc=38156]\n- a trooper [npc=38157]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Lunanyn #2: The Assassination Game [quest=5418]\n- Lunanyn #3: Uncharted Territory [quest=5419]\n- Lunanyn #4: The Enemy of My Enemy [quest=5420]\n- Lunanyn #5: The Memory Remains [quest=5421]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 15 17:31:48 2011\nModified: Fri Mar 11 02:00:08 2022 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the first in a series of five; a solo task that begins with Geirdan Ath in the Valley of Lunanyn, located at 2295, -1700, 46 (in a building in the southeast part of the upper section of the zone)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- (no minimum required skill level in Alaran Language)\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Geirdan Ath'\nGeirdan Ath says 'You are not one of mine! But you can be of use to me! We have [lost] many men recently and are unable to stop the Prophet's Army from raiding the crops here.'\nYou say, 'How were they lost?'\nGeirdan Ath says 'Most of them have been killed in battle, but we are missing some that were on patrol. They seem to have vanished without a trace. I suspect the Prophet's Army is to blame. They are struggling to take the [crops] here to support their army and it is only a matter of time before they will outlast us.'\nYou say, 'What about the crops?'\nGeirdan Ath says 'They take the crops from their own people, who hide in fear from their own army. Will you [help] us?'\nYou say, 'I'll help'\nGeirdan Ath says 'Excellent! I will see to it that you rewarded should your efforts prove successful!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Raid and Recover'.\nGeirdan Ath is spread thin until reinforcements arrive. He will need you to seek out the Erillion Army raiding parties and put a stop to their taking of the local crops. You will need to be careful during your engagements as the Prophet's army has been taking prisoners for a reason that Geirdan has yet to ascertain. He would also like you to find the soldiers that have gone missing.\nYou must slow down the Prophet's army from taking the crops to their troops.\n\n---\n\nFind the camp that is keeping the soldiers hostage 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_This is the large camp in the southern end of the zone, you can find it at /waypoint -994, 395, -40. You can update this step invis._\nKill 5 troopers 0/5 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak with a missing soldier 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak with a missing soldier 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak with a missing soldier 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nSpeak with a missing soldier 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\na missing soldier says 'Thank you! I knew someone would come help me!'\na missing soldier says 'You sure took your time freeing me didn't you?'\na missing soldier says 'These Alaran scum will get what's coming to them if it's the last thing I do!'\na missing soldier says 'I knew the Geirdan wouldn't forget about me! I am his right hand man after all.'\n_The missing soldiers are found in the tents in the same camp._\nSpeak with Geirdan Ath 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nYou say, 'Hail, Geirdan Ath'\nGeirdan Ath says 'You have returned! Your efforts to stop the raiding of the crops will help greatly. Though, I am concerned that we were unable to find out why they are taking my men. '\nYou were able to put a stop to the raiders and have freed the missing soldiers, at least until their reinforcements can arrive.\n_Rewards:_\n106 platinum\nExperience\nEltarki's Diary - Life and Death\n- Eltarki's Diary - Life and Death [item=98146]",
