      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Valley of Lunanyn [zone=807]\n**Who:**\n- Captain Gre Metkal [npc=38148]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 90\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Forged Orders [item=100735]\n- Orders of the Prophet [item=99810]\n- Poison of the Huntsman [item=100000]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Aedros [npc=38155]\n- Pika [npc=38267]\n- a deadly huntsman [npc=38278]\n- a trooper [npc=38157]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Lunanyn #1: Raid and Recover [quest=5395]\n- Lunanyn #2: The Assassination Game [quest=5418]\n- Lunanyn #3: Uncharted Territory [quest=5419]\n- Lunanyn #5: The Memory Remains [quest=5421]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Nov 16 02:38:51 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This task is the fourth in a series of five; a solo task that begins with Captain Gre Metkal in the Valley of Lunanyn (Rallosian camp in northeastern part of the lower section of the zone)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"Raid and Recover\"\n\\- Completion of \"The Assassination Game\"\n\\- Completion of \"Uncharted Territory\"\n\\- (no minimum required skill level in Alaran Language)\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Gre Metkal'\nCaptain Gre Metkal says 'I have an idea. It will require a bit of [subterfuge] on your part, but should you be successful, it will help in removing the wraiths of Arelis village as another participant in the upcoming battles.'\nYou say, 'Subterfuge?'\nCaptain Gre Metkal says 'The wraiths seem to blame us for the destruction of their village. It seems to me that if their anger can be [redirected] to the Prophet army it will remove one obstacle from our efforts in controlling the valley.'\nYou say, 'Redirected?'\nCaptain Gre Metkal says 'Tell them whatever you like. I care little. You just need to get it done. Is this something that you can handle, or should I seek someone more [capable] to help Rallos?'\nYou say, 'I'm capable'\nCaptain Gre Metkal says 'Excellent! I will see to it that you rewarded should your efforts prove successful!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Enemy of My Enemy'.\nCaptain Gre Metkal believes it is important to get the wraiths of Arelis Village on his side of this war. Even if the wraiths do nothing more than agree to not attack the Rallosian army, it will be one less thing he will need to worry about.\nThe wraith Aedros is the leader of the former inhabitants of Arelis Village.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Aedros 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_Aedros spawns in the undead camp in the east-central part of the zone (about -155, -515)._\nKill troopers while searching for evidence 0/5 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_Task Window Says:_ You need proof that the Prophet's army is responsible for the destruction of the village. It is possible that Erillion troopers may have evidence on them.\n_Kill five more troopers in the southern camp or in the farm area to the north._\nSpeak with Captain Gre Metkal 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_Task Window Says:_ You have found nothing to tie the Prophet's army to the destruction of Arelis village. Captain Gre Metkal may know what to do next.\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Gre Metkal'\nCaptain Gre Metkal says 'So, it wants proof? It will have its proof! Go to the foothill in the south and find Pika. He is a recluse that I have had dealings with early on. He will help you.'\nSpeak with Pika 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_Task Window Says:_ According to Captain Metkal, the recluse, Pika, may be able to help. He loves to hide near the caves to the south.\n_Pika spawns above the cave in the southwestern part of the zone (-1100, 1300)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Pika'\nPika says 'You Norrathians always come to Pika! Not know what is... worse, you or them Prophet army thugs! What do you... [want]?'\nYou say, 'I don't want anything; Gre Metkal sent me!'\nPika says 'The Captain sent you?! Of course! Come now... What can Pika do for the [Captain]?'\nYou say, 'You can do a lot for the captain...'\nPika says 'That is all? Pika can do... um... easy! You need to find Pika some official order of the Prophet. Pika not know where to get, you just get. Bring that to me and Pika can... begin!'\nLoot the Orders of the Prophet from an Erillion soldier 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_These drop from the same mobs in the trooper camp._\nDeliver the Orders of the Prophet to Pika 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\nPika says 'This will do just fine. Now Pika will need you to get the poison from a huntsman. But it must be a mature huntsman! Not from those baby ones!'\nLoot a Poison of the Huntsman 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_These drop from higher level huntsman spiders in the zone (Level 95+)._\nDeliver the poison to Pika 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Great care must be taken when handling the highly corrosive poison that is sometimes used to make etchings in skin and parchment.\nPika says 'Very good! Pika needs just a... moment. Here are the orders the Captain needs. Tell the Captain that Pika help any time!'\nTake the Forged Orders to Aedros 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_Task Window Says:_ These new orders from Pika should be enough to convince Aedros that the Prophet's army was involved in the destruction of Arelis village.\nSpeak with Captain Gre Metkal 0/1 (Valley of Lunanyn)\n_Task Window Says:_ Captain Gre Metkal will want to know the outcome of his ruse.\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Gre Metkal'\nCaptain Gre Metkal says 'You have done well. I have to say that I am more than a little surprised that it worked. Thank you for your help. '\n_Rewards:_\nEltarki's Diary - Life and Death\n213 platinum\nExperience\n- Eltarki's Diary - Life and Death [item=98146]",
    },
